.TH EXECVE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
execve \- replace the process image
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B int execve(const char* path, char* const* arguments, char* const* environment);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Replaces the current process with the executable at path. Arguments and
environment are separately NULL\-terminated vectors. Linux executable,
descriptor and signal\-disposition rules apply.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Does not return on success. On failure returns \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fork (3crunch),
.BR execve (2)
